namespace pdg { /**
\fn pdg::Animated::grow(number factor, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Multiply logical width and height by one factor.

The overload without duration applies immediately and preserves growth rates. A timed request replaces growth. With andThen(), the factor is applied to size at the start of the operation. Transform scale remains unchanged. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param factor Multiplicative factor for logical size.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see stretch(), resizeBy(), setGrowing()
*/
 }
